From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wbemprox: grow the service list until it fits

Found by the conformance comparison (wbemprox query, wbemdisp: Win32_Service
"not available"; also main's gates wbemproc and jscript): fast-a 3155 made
EnumServicesStatusEx answer as Windows does, partial results and the bytes
needed for the services NOT returned. fill_service started with 256 bytes
and retried from the start with only "needed" bytes, which is too little
now, so the Win32_Service table always failed to fill. The buffer now
grows until every service fits.

Mutant: SG_MUTANT_WMI_SVC_NEEDED_ONLY (wbemproc gate).
---
diff --git a/dlls/wbemprox/builtin.c b/dlls/wbemprox/builtin.c
--- a/dlls/wbemprox/builtin.c
+++ b/dlls/wbemprox/builtin.c
@@ -5263,19 +5263,30 @@ static enum fill_status fill_service( struct table *table, const struct expr *co
     if (!(manager = OpenSCManagerW( NULL, NULL, SC_MANAGER_ENUMERATE_SERVICE ))) return FILL_STATUS_FAILED;
     if (!(services = malloc( size ))) goto done;
 
-    ret = EnumServicesStatusExW( manager, SC_ENUM_PROCESS_INFO, SERVICE_TYPE_ALL,
-                                 SERVICE_STATE_ALL, (BYTE *)services, size, &needed,
-                                 &count, NULL, NULL );
-    if (!ret)
+    /* Stained Glass OS: with a buffer that is too small, the bytes needed are those of the
+     * services not returned (fast-a 3155, as on Windows), so a retry from the start needs
+     * room for what came back too: grow until everything fits */
+    for (;;)
     {
+        ret = EnumServicesStatusExW( manager, SC_ENUM_PROCESS_INFO, SERVICE_TYPE_ALL,
+                                     SERVICE_STATE_ALL, (BYTE *)services, size, &needed,
+                                     &count, NULL, NULL );
+        if (ret) break;
         if (GetLastError() != ERROR_MORE_DATA) goto done;
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_WMI_SVC_NEEDED_ONLY
         size = needed;
+#else
+        size += needed;
+#endif
         if (!(tmp = realloc( services, size ))) goto done;
         services = tmp;
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_WMI_SVC_NEEDED_ONLY
         ret = EnumServicesStatusExW( manager, SC_ENUM_PROCESS_INFO, SERVICE_TYPE_ALL,
                                      SERVICE_STATE_ALL, (BYTE *)services, size, &needed,
                                      &count, NULL, NULL );
         if (!ret) goto done;
+        break;
+#endif
     }
     if (!resize_table( table, count, sizeof(*rec) )) goto done;
 
